## 3. Notes on Baseline (`B0 + B1 + B2`) Verification

- **Why `[PROFILE]` shows 22 dispatches (vs 21 prior to `d6f70fb`)**:
  - Commit `d6f70fb` lowered `D3dDevice::fill`'s upload-ring `staged()` threshold to `<= 256` bytes so the per-frame 50 KB `flow_` clear (`Engine::record_net`) executes via GPU `clear_range.spv` (`~1.5 us`) instead of a PCIe DMA copy. `[PROFILE]` reports both `sum` (all 22 dispatches) and `net21_sum` (the 21 network/post dispatches excluding `clear_range.spv`).
- **B0 & K2 Deterministic SPIR-V Hash Gate**:
  - `test_asi_units.exe` computes the FNV-1a 64-bit hash of the 5 shipped Top-5 SPIR-V binaries in `build/asi/stage/openrr-amd/shaders/` and asserts `h_ship == h_nopad && h_ship != h_pad16k` (`spv_hash_nopad=EXACT`), deterministically catching any accidental re-enablement of `LDS_OCC_PAD`.
- **B1 Isolated Lossless Fast-Mode Pooling in `t0` (`attr_` Tail) + Wide Path + Negative Control**:
  - Because `enc2 .. dec2_1` execute concurrently without barriers in flow mode, `enc_l_[1].pooled` and `enc_l_[1].dfn_pool` at the start of `f0` remain live during the flow chain. Placing `dec1_l_[2..4].tensor` and `dec1_l_[1..4].dfn` in the unused tail of `t0` (`px0 * 42.4 .. px0 * 46.6 < px0 * 48`, after all `enc_l_[1..5]` sub-buffers and `dec1_l_[1].tensor`, and above `dec_head_32_64`'s `px0 * 40` `headScratch`) avoids any address overlap with live flow inputs.
  - Also fixed `dec0ScratchBytes` sizing to include the starting offset of `enc_l_[0].dfn_pool` (`enc0DfnPoolEnd = align256(dec0ScratchBytes) + px0 / 4 * 8`) and fixed `wide` attribute allocation (`attr_wide_`) so it allocates a separate zero-initialized buffer without destroying `attr_` in the middle of command-list recording.
  - Verified in isolation (same binary, `set_pool_dec1_tail(false)` vs `set_pool_dec1_tail(true)` across 20 frames x 2 runs, with frames 10..14 exercising the `wide` `depth_of_field` path, plus a negative-control run `set_pool_dec1_f0_race_for_test(true)` that restores the `0dc2625` `f0+0` layout):
    - 1080p: `diff_vs_unpooled=0 (max_ulp_diff=0), repeat_diff=0, flow_overlap_audit=CLEAN (neg_ctrl_f0_race_caught=YES, race_diff=57188637), saved=1.44 MB` (`252 -> 251 MB` feature, `-2.3 MB` `proc_delta`).
    - 4K: `diff_vs_unpooled=0 (max_ulp_diff=0), repeat_diff=0, flow_overlap_audit=CLEAN (neg_ctrl_f0_race_caught=YES, race_diff=227910767), saved=5.62 MB` (`966 -> 960 MB` feature, `-6.7 MB` `proc_delta`).
- **B2 Lossy Fast-Mode Approximations & 3-Run Per-Macro A/B**:
  - 3-run interleaved per-macro A/B in `test_asi_units.exe` confirms:
    - `post_f_lt`: `+LT_POST_EXP=1 +LT_POST_NOCORNER=1 +LT_POST_NETH=1` improves 1080p 3-run median by `-5.7%` (`346.4 -> 326.6 us`, `-19.8 us`) and 4K 3-run median by `-6.0%` (`1503.2 -> 1412.6 us`, `-90.6 us`), whereas adding `LT_POST_LOG=1` slows down 1080p by `+6.5%` (`348.0 us`) and 4K by `+6.2%` (`1499.8 us`). **Enabled by default.**
    - `enc0_attr_f_lt`: `+LT_ATTR_RCP=1 +LT_ATTR_DEPTH=1` is within noise (`+1.8%` at 1080p `178.0 -> 181.2 us`, `-1.6%` at 4K `835.1 -> 822.0 us` with overlapping min/max ranges `[826.0..839.8]` vs `[819.5..836.7]`), while `+LT_ATTR_SAME=1 +LT_ATTR_CL=1` slows down 1080p by `+33.6%` (`242.1 us`) and 4K by `+20.1%` (`987.2 us`). **Both disabled by default** per the rule that a lossy macro must clearly speed up both 1080p and 4K.
    - `C=64` (`enc_stage_64_64_96` + `dec_up_64_64_96` + `dec_dfn_64_64`): `+LT_FAR=3` is within noise at 1080p (`-0.3%`, `711.6 -> 709.7 us`) and slower at 4K (`+1.3%`, `2670.4 -> 2704.8 us`). **Disabled by default.**
  - **Kernel vs End-to-End Delta Reconciliation**:
    - With only `LT_POST_EXP=1 LT_POST_NOCORNER=1 LT_POST_NETH=1` enabled (plus `B0` removing `LDS_OCC_PAD=8192` from W1), at 1080p `post_f_lt` saves `~20 us` (`346.4 -> 326.6 us`), while removing `LDS_OCC_PAD=8192` from W1 (where 1080p working set fits in Infinity Cache) costs `~0-5 us` (`W1` `nopad=1023.7 us` vs `occ_pad_16KB=1018.0 us`), and end-to-end 3-run median improves by **`-47 us` (`3.171 -> 3.124 ms`, `-1.5%`)**.
    - At 4K, `post_f_lt` saves `~91 us` (`1503.2 -> 1412.6 us`) and removing `LDS_OCC_PAD=8192` from W1 saves `~60 us` (`4197.9 -> 4137.7 us`), totaling `~151 us` at the kernel level, while end-to-end 3-run median improves by **`-122 us` (`11.941 -> 11.824 ms`, `-1.0%`; Run 3: `11.966 -> 11.749 ms`, `-217 us` / `-1.8%`)**.

